---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import MarsHeroVideo from '../components/MarsHeroVideo.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Mars"
  description="Mars overview plus a practical snapshot of SpaceX's public plan to send cargo and eventually people to Mars."
>
  <section class="page-home-hero">
    <MarsHeroVideo />
    <div class="page-home-hero-inner">
      <p class="page-home-hero-eyebrow">Red Planet</p>
      <h1 class="page-home-hero-heading">Mars and the SpaceX plan</h1>
      <p class="page-home-hero-lead">
        Cargo-first missions, orbital refilling, and a long timeline toward crewed surface operations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pb-24 md:px-8">
    <PageHero
      eyebrow="Mission context"
      title="What the plan actually depends on"
      subtitle="Mars is the long-game target for human expansion beyond Earth. Here is the plain-language version of what SpaceX says it is trying to build, and what still has to work first."
    />

    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-void-850/40 p-6 md:p-8">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-white">Why Mars?</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate-300">
          Mars has day length close to Earth, accessible water ice in several regions, and enough gravity to make long
          surface operations more practical than microgravity habitats. It is still extremely hostile—thin atmosphere,
          radiation, dust, and cold—but it is one of the few worlds where a large, sustained human presence is
          considered plausible.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-void-850/40 p-6 md:p-8">
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-white">SpaceX architecture (publicly stated)</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-400">
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> <strong class="text-slate-300">Starship + Super Heavy</strong> as a fully reusable transport stack</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> <strong class="text-slate-300">On-orbit refilling</strong> in low Earth orbit before Mars departure</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> <strong class="text-slate-300">Cargo-first campaigns</strong> to land equipment ahead of crew</li>
          <li><span class="text-nebula">•</span> <strong class="text-slate-300">Transfer-window cadence</strong> tied to Earth-Mars alignments (~26 months)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-nebula/20 bg-nebula/5 p-6 md:p-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-white">What has to be true before crewed Mars flights</h2>
      <ol class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-300">
        <li><span class="text-nebula">1.</span> Repeated, reliable Starship launches and recoveries</li>
        <li><span class="text-nebula">2.</span> High-confidence orbital propellant transfer at operational scale</li>
        <li><span class="text-nebula">3.</span> Robust entry, descent, and landing performance at Mars</li>
        <li><span class="text-nebula">4.</span> Surface power, comms, and life-support logistics that survive long missions</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-400">
        Timelines are aspirational and can shift. Treat dates as targets, not guarantees.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-void-850/40 p-6 md:p-8">
      <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold text-white">Sources and tracking</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-slate-300">
        For the current public posture, check official pages first and then compare with launch results and mission
        updates.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.spacex.com/vehicles/starship/"
            class="text-nebula underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >SpaceX Starship page</a
          >
          (design goals, Mars mission statements, refilling concept)
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.nasa.gov/humans-in-space/moon-to-mars/"
            class="text-nebula underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >NASA Moon to Mars</a
          >
          (agency-level exploration context)
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/edu/resources/lesson-plan/lets-go-to-mars-calculating-launch-windows/"
            class="text-nebula underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >JPL launch-window explainer</a
          >
          (why Earth-Mars windows recur about every 26 months)
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
